course: dictionary
lesson: 12451
title: Deepening: deeper, stronger or lower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deepening comes from deep, so it often means becoming deeper. But the word can also mean becoming stronger, more serious or more intense. You can find out which meaning fits by reading the words around it. «The river has been deepening its valley for thousands of years.» Here the river is cutting further down into the land.
explain: Look at the context to choose the right meaning. «The clues piled up, and the mystery was deepening.» The clues make the mystery more puzzling and serious, so deepening means growing more intense. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «the mystery was getting more serious» still make sense? It does.
explain: Deepening can also describe a sound that becomes lower. «His voice was deepening as he grew older.» A voice that gets deeper sounds lower, not louder. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, check which one fits the whole sentence.
fact: Deepening means becoming or making something deeper.
fact: Deepening can also mean becoming stronger, more serious or more intense.
fact: «A deepening mystery» means a mystery that gets more puzzling as you learn more.
fact: «The deepening dusk» means the evening getting darker.
fact: Rivers deepen their valleys over time, and the sea gets deeper further from the shore.
exercise: «The river has been deepening its valley for thousands of years.» What is the river doing? | Drying up completely | Turning into a lake overnight | Flowing uphill | *Making its valley deeper
exercise: «The detective felt a deepening mystery as the clues piled up.» What does deepening mean here? | Getting shorter | Being solved quickly | Getting shallower | *Getting more puzzling and serious
exercise: «The deepening dusk crept over the fields.» What is getting deeper here? | *The evening getting darker | The fields getting wetter | The birds getting louder | The sun getting bigger
test: «Their friendship was deepening every week they spent together.» What does deepening mean? | Moving further away | Getting weaker | Forgetting each other | *Growing stronger and closer
test: «His voice was deepening as he grew up.» What does deepening show? | The voice is getting faster | *The voice is getting lower | The voice is getting louder | The voice has stopped
exam: The boat sailed out, and the water was deepening under its keel. What does deepening mean? | Getting more shallow | Getting warmer | Getting bluer | *Getting deeper
